# Data pulled by the collectors here. Not committed: the paths file alone is
# 109 MB, and the collectors rebuild all of it from Alpaca.
# The CONTENTS rather than the directory: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation for a file inside it can never re-include the file.
data/*
# and the same name as a symlink, which neither of the above matches
data
# The exceptions, which are the point of `make claims`: everything the published
# numbers are recomputed from. Without it every number this project publishes needs
# a credential to check. `collect_exits.py` rebuilds them; they are committed so
# that nobody has to.
#
# The negations below do NOT work on their own, and one file was missing from the
# repository for days because of it: `data` above excludes the directory itself,
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, and a negation for a file inside
# one can never re-include it. Each of these was added with `git add -f` and is
# tracked; the lines are here to say which files belong in the repository.
!data/candidates_bt.parquet
!data/stock_*_15m.json
!data/stock_*_day.json
!data/contracts_*.json
!data/obars_*.jsonl
!data/buyback_lows.json
!data/daily.parquet
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
